# A finite graph, modeled concretely and proved to satisfy the defining graph properties by the kernel. The example is the
# triangle (the 3-cycle): three nodes, each adjacent to the other two. The kernel proves the adjacency is SYMMETRIC (the
# graph is undirected, the property the mesh shares: every edge is two-way) and IRREFLEXIVE (no node is adjacent to
# itself, no self-loops), by exhaustive induction over the nodes, and checks the handshake lemma (the degrees sum to twice
# the edge count). This is the graph-theoretic core the mesh is an instance of: the hyperbolic honeycomb is an undirected
# 24-regular graph, and its navigation and addressing rest on exactly these properties.

# The three nodes of the triangle.
form node
  case n0
  case n1
  case n2

form flag
  case yes
  case no

# TEMPLATE: one entry of the adjacency table. For a fixed second node `col`, send the yes or no answer. One definition
# replaces every near-identical `case .. / send back / make ..` block.
tree adjacent-entry
  take col
  take answer

  hook fuse
    case {col}
      send back
        make {answer}

# Adjacency in the triangle: two nodes are adjacent exactly when they are different (every pair of distinct nodes shares
# an edge). Given directly as the table over the nine node pairs.
task adjacent
  take a, like node
  take b, like node
  like flag
  fork case, read a
    case n0
      fork case, read b
        fuse adjacent-entry, n0, no
        fuse adjacent-entry, n1, yes
        fuse adjacent-entry, n2, yes
    case n1
      fork case, read b
        fuse adjacent-entry, n0, yes
        fuse adjacent-entry, n1, no
        fuse adjacent-entry, n2, yes
    case n2
      fork case, read b
        fuse adjacent-entry, n0, yes
        fuse adjacent-entry, n1, yes
        fuse adjacent-entry, n2, no

# ADJACENCY IS SYMMETRIC: adjacent a b = adjacent b a, the graph is UNDIRECTED. Over all nine node pairs.
rule adjacent-is-symmetric
  seat a, like node
  seat b, like node
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call adjacent
        read a
        read b
      call adjacent
        read b
        read a
  fold a, b

# ADJACENCY IS IRREFLEXIVE: adjacent a a = no, no node is adjacent to itself (no self-loops). Over the three nodes.
rule adjacent-is-irreflexive
  seat a, like node
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call adjacent
        read a
        read a
      make no
  fold a

# THE HANDSHAKE LEMMA: the sum of the degrees equals twice the number of edges. The triangle has three nodes each of
# degree two, summing to six, and three edges, and 3 * 2 = 6 = 2 * 3. Every edge is counted once at each of its ends.
hold handshake-degree-sum-is-twice-edges
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 2
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 3
